{"lines": ["He shot the first known film. Then he boarded a train, and vanished.", "Dijon, 1890. Louis Le Prince waves goodbye to his brother Albert, carrying a suitcase said to hold his patents.", "Two years earlier, in a garden in Leeds, he filmed what is believed to be the oldest surviving motion picture.", "Next, he was due in New York to show his moving pictures to the public.", "Friends wait in Paris. But when the train arrives, he isn't on it.", "He stood six foot four, yet not one passenger reported seeing him aboard.", "French police and Scotland Yard search the line. No body. No suitcase. Nothing.", "Seven years later, he is declared dead.", "His wife blames his patent rival, Thomas Edison.", "Then, in 2003, a photo surfaces in Paris police files: a man drowned in 1890 who looks like him.", "Too short, though, for a man his height.", "Others suspect the brother who saw him last, after a row over their mother's will.", "Edison, or the brother who put him on that train?"], "words": [["He", 0.0, 0.08], ["shot", 0.08, 0.32], ["the", 0.32, 0.52], ["first", 0.52, 0.76], ["known", 0.76, 1.0], ["film.", 1.0, 1.36], ["Then", 1.72, 1.84], ["he", 1.84, 1.92], ["boarded", 1.92, 2.16], ["a", 2.16, 2.34], ["train,", 2.34, 2.62], ["and", 2.62, 2.96], ["vanished.", 2.96, 3.32], ["Dijon,", 3.68, 4.16], ["1890.", 4.16, 4.64], ["Louis", 5.0, 5.2], ["Le", 5.2, 5.4], ["Prince", 5.4, 5.58], ["waves", 5.58, 6.0], ["goodbye", 6.0, 6.22], ["to", 6.22, 6.66], ["his", 6.66, 6.78], ["brother", 6.78, 6.96], ["Albert,", 6.96, 7.34], ["carrying", 7.6, 7.94], ["a", 7.94, 8.14], ["suitcase", 8.14, 8.36], ["said", 8.36, 8.9], ["to", 8.9, 9.06], ["hold", 9.06, 9.26], ["his", 9.26, 9.46], ["patents.", 9.46, 9.8], ["Two", 10.16, 10.25], ["years", 10.25, 10.45], ["earlier,", 10.45, 10.81], ["in", 11.09, 11.19], ["a", 11.19, 11.27], ["garden", 11.27, 11.57], ["in", 11.57, 11.81], ["Leeds,", 11.81, 12.37], ["he", 12.63, 12.71], ["filmed", 12.71, 12.91], ["what", 12.91, 13.19], ["is", 13.19, 13.3